/datum/patron/divine/abyssor
	desc = "Abyssor is many things; sire of the Seaborne, imposer of the Change. Worship of the Deep Will varies greatly across the Known World- from cherishing the bounty of the ocean, praying for the safe return of fleets afloat, and - even in the arid deserts of Raneshan - praying for change so driven by the Dreamer Divine; be it a new turn in a person’s life, cultural shifts, or rightful societal upheaval. Like a river, fate flows; His many hands carve its course. \n\nStagnation is to be scorned. The waves will always welcome you."

/datum/patron/divine/dendor
	desc = "Dendor is a voice that speaks through the creak and rustle of trees. His flesh is that of the prey; His blood coursing hotly through the predator. It is he whose dreams are caught in fungus; capable of being consumed and shared. Those strongest attuned to Him discard all trappings of the civil and settled; throwing their lives away to exist free, faceless, to live, breed, eat, and die in the Wildman’s beautiful Cycle.\n\nAmong more settled, civilized believers, the Treefather paradoxically serves as both a force of rabid, animistic chaos - and stable, steady growth. To a new mother, she offers tidings to Dendor for the safe keeping of her babes; that they may grow up healthy and resplendent- as so many of His groves do. Even a merchant deep within the cities of the world may pray to the Hamadryad– seeking a secure growth to his coffers and marketplace.\n\nThere is so much wisdom in the Wild; why do you not seek it?"

/datum/patron/divine/astrata
	desc = "The Tyrant of the Gods, sister and counterpart to Noc. Greatest of the Living Gods. She, the Radiance, burns away the evils at bay during the dae; and has defined the rights of society for nearly two millennia."

/datum/patron/divine/noc
	desc = "The Reflective Will - and counterpart to Astrata, aside. In contrast to Solar Will, whose law and diction is absolute, Noc is best described as somewhere between a mirror and a conduit- offering wisdom, insight, wonder and thaumic empowerment to all who look upon them. They share freely what could be learned - and the only judgement cast is the onlooker's own."

/datum/patron/divine/undivided
	desc = "Five Eternal, Divine Pantheon United, Bulwark against the Darkness. The Five True Divines diligently watch over their flock granting them potent boons, but not every man catches the attention of merely one. Take lessons from them all, for they are your masters and mentors."
	worshippers = "Commonfolk, Zybantines, Raneshani, the Clergy, and Nobility"
	confess_lines = list(
		"THE HOLY PENTACLE SHALL SHIELD MY SOUL!",
		"I SERVE THE PANTHEON RESPLENDENT!",
		"THE FIVE ETERNAL, FOREVERMORE!",
	)
	titles = list(
		"Gods"
	)
